React Development Rules

Code Style and Structure
======================

- Write functional React components using arrow functions
- Utilize React Hooks (`useState`, `useEffect`, `useContext`, etc.)
- Follow consistent code formatting (e.g., using Prettier)
- Utilize ESLint with React-specific rules
- Organize components into logical directories based on features
- Use descriptive names for components, variables, and props
- Pass data down using props and handle state updates appropriately
- Implement proper error handling within components

Component Design and Usage
========================

- Design reusable and composable components with well-defined props
- Follow the single responsibility principle for components
- Use keys effectively when rendering lists of elements
- Implement controlled components for form elements
- Lift state up to the lowest common ancestor when needed
- Utilize context API or state management libraries appropriately
- Optimize component rendering using `React.memo`

Asynchronous Operations
=====================

- Use `useEffect` Hook for handling side effects
- Clean up side effects within the `useEffect` cleanup function
- Handle asynchronous data fetching and loading states

UI and User Experience
====================

- Follow established UI/UX best practices and design principles
- Ensure components are responsive and adapt to screen sizes
- Provide clear and informative feedback to users
- Implement proper accessibility (ARIA attributes, keyboard navigation)

React Performance
===============

- Minimize unnecessary re-renders using proper techniques
- Optimize component structure and avoid deep nesting
- Implement code splitting to reduce bundle size
- Use lazy loading for components and assets
- Optimize images and other assets

